# Hardware Connections and Circuit Description

## 1. Overview

The prototype uses an ESP32 development board as the main processing unit. It receives electrical measurements from the connected sensors, processes the data, identifies abnormal operating conditions, and communicates the system status to the user.

The prototype is implemented using a low-voltage DC supply for demonstration and testing.

## 2. Hardware Components

| Component                  | Function                                      |
| -------------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |
| ESP32 development board    | Main controller and Wi-Fi communication       |
| Voltage sensor             | Measures the supply voltage                   |
| Current sensor             | Measures the current flowing through the load |
| Temperature sensor         | Monitors temperature                          |
| 0.96-inch I2C OLED display | Displays measurements and system status       |
| DC power supply            | Supplies power to the prototype               |
| Load resistor              | Acts as the electrical load                   |
| Connecting wires           | Establish electrical connections              |

## 3. Circuit Connections

The ESP32 is connected to the voltage, current, and temperature sensors. The sensor outputs are processed by the microcontroller.

The OLED display communicates with the ESP32 through the I2C interface.

The prototype uses a DC supply and a suitable load to demonstrate electrical monitoring and fault detection.

